# Test (built by ./dash straight to hunk; by ./dash --gcc: test_image_decode_salida.dash): a program that ends
# while image_decode_start decodes does not wait for the whole picture (the decode stops), and the picture it
# decoded but never took comes back (Tachyon ending with an abort while YouTube's
# pictures decoded: it waited for each of them, seconds at 94 % of the CPU, and their memory stayed taken).
# The program makes an 800 x 600 grey PNG in RAM:, decodes it once to know how long it takes (3 s on the A1200),
# and runs itself twice: "hijo" starts a decode and ends at once; "hijo2" waits until the picture is decoded (1.4 MB
# taken) and ends without image_decode_finish. Where a decode takes under a second and a half (a fast machine), the
# time says nothing.
# dash-direct:
# expect-out: decodificada: true
# expect-out: el hijo no esperó a la imagen: true
# expect-out: hijo2: la imagen ocupa memoria: true
# expect-out: memoria devuelta: true
# expect-out: fin

import "lib/salida_imagen.dash"

Main
    prueba_salida()
end
